      "summary": "Saudi Arabia's Hajj Minister reported that more than 860,000 foreign pilgrims had arrived in the kingdom by mid-week for the 2026 Hajj season, with the government mobilizing extensive logistical, transport, and digital operations. The minister attributed preparations to directives from King Salman and Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wife of British-Saudi detainee Ahmed al-Doush appeals for release as health declines",
      "summary": "The wife of Ahmed al-Doush, a British national imprisoned in Saudi Arabia since 2024 for social media posts, publicly appealed for his release as his health reportedly deteriorates sharply. The UN Working Group on Arbitrary Detention published a report in March 2026 recommending his release, but Saudi Arabia in April confirmed his conviction, reducing his sentence while describing the posts as terrorist-related content."
    },
    {
      "headline": "EFF launches campaign for imprisoned Saudi Wikipedian Osama Khalid",
      "summary": "The Electronic Frontier Foundation launched a new advocacy campaign for Osama Khalid, a Saudi Arabian Wikipedia contributor and blogger imprisoned for his writing on Saudi Arabia, open source technology, and other topics. The EFF described the case as emblematic of the kingdom's pattern of jailing online speech."
    },
    {
      "headline": "MBS receives delegation honoring King Salman's 60+ years of Quran memorization patronage",
      "summary": "Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman received a delegation honoring King Salman for his more than 60 years of support for Holy Quran memorization associations across the Kingdom. The delegation presented gifts including a luxury shield, a handwritten Quran copy, and commemorative plaques."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Saudi deputy FM attends Uganda presidential inauguration on behalf of Crown Prince",
      "summary": "Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs Waleed Al-Kheraiji attended the inauguration of Ugandan President Yoweri Museveni in Kampala on behalf of Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman. During the ceremony, Al-Kheraiji conveyed congratulations from King Salman and the Crown Prince."
    }
  ]
